  data:  # 056b
    kind: invariant  # 056b
    title: "A PR description is not a commit message: the de-branding scrub is a git hook, so the session URL is published verbatim to the forge API"  # 056b
    status: needs_human_review  # 056b
    priority: 2  # 056b
    parent:  # 056b
    tags:  # 056b
    - governance  # 056b
    - hooks  # 056b
    - privacy  # 056b
    isbefore: []  # 056b
    duplicate_of: []  # 056b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 056b
    pr_ref:  # 056b
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-26 by the owner, who noticed that a PR message is not a commit\nmessage. It is not a reopening of INV-kunot: that item's statement is scoped to\nCOMMIT MESSAGES and is correctly satisfied. This is the same fact in a second\nhome the statement never named.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. `commit-msg` is a GIT hook. A PR description is handed to the\nforge over the HTTP API and never passes through git at all, so no git hook can\nreach it. Measured: `scripts/auto-pr`, `scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh` and\n`scripts/merge-pr` contain ZERO occurrences of brand / scrub / absurd /\ndebrand. The description string goes from the caller to `create_pr` untouched.\n\nTHE LEAK, observed live on PR #556. The harness appends a session trailer to\nboth artifacts. On the COMMIT it was scrubbed exactly as designed:\n\n  Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_<id>\n    -> Racial-Capitalism-Is-Bad: a VHS-headed magpie sipping a tea in a\n       neon-brontosaurus lounge with a robot waiter made of black bread crusts\n\nOn the PR DESCRIPTION for the same change, the identical URL was published\nverbatim to a public GitHub pull request.\n\nWHY THIS DEFEATS THE RULING THAT CLOSED INV-kunot rather than merely sitting\noutside it. That ruling forced the trailer VALUE through the rewriter even when\nthe value looked innocuous, and the recorded reason was that a scrubbed key\nover an intact value \"would still publish the session id it points at\". The\nsession id is the protected thing. The PR body publishes it.\n\nACCRUAL, which is what made INV-kunot urgent and applies here unchanged: that\nitem measured \"not a static set of historical commits, it grew by one per\ncommit until fixed\". This grows by one per PR. #556 carries it now; #548, #552\nand #553 were authored the same way (drafts verified, posted bodies not).\n\nOWNER RULING 2026-08-26, verbatim: \"the scrub belongs in auto-pr\".\n\nSO THE FIX IS PLACEMENT, NOT DESIGN -- the rewriter already exists and is\nalready ratified. What is owed is that `auto-pr` route the description through\nit before handing it to `create_pr`, so the two artifacts of one change are\nscrubbed by one rule.\n\nDESIGN QUESTIONS THIS ITEM MUST ANSWER, none of them settled here:\n  * WHICH surfaces: --description on do_pr, the flush_queue path, the vPR\n    queue payload, and the PR TITLE as well as the body.\n  * The scrub logic lives in `.githooks/commit-msg` as shell. Sharing it with\n    `scripts/auto-pr` means extracting it to a common home rather than growing\n    a SECOND copy -- a second copy is the exact defect shape this project has\n    repeatedly paid for (LIVE.md: one fact, two homes, the second silently\n    wins). `.githooks/brand-patterns.txt` and `.githooks/absurd-phrases.txt`\n    are already data files and can be read from either caller.\n  * INV-kunot's own false-positive finding carries over intact: the pattern\n    list contains ordinary English words, and `falcon` is a web framework THIS\n    PROJECT SUPPORTS. A PR body discussing falcon routing would be mangled.\n    The owner's recorded mitigation was to limit the scan to roughly the first\n    and last 10 lines. A PR body is much longer than a commit message, so that\n    window matters MORE here, not less.\n  * Whether already-published PR bodies (#548, #552, #553, #556) should be\n    edited. Editing is a forge API write and needs its own authorisation.\n\nGOVERNANCE: `scripts/auto-pr`, `scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh` and `.githooks/**`\nall require human approval. Filed at needs_human_review; the placement is ruled\nbut the surface list, the sharing mechanism and the false-positive window are\nnot."  # 056b
    fields:  # 056b
      statement: "An artifact published from this repo must not carry a vendor brand or a session identifier in any position, whatever channel publishes it. This holds for commit messages via the commit-msg hook and fails for PR titles and descriptions, which reach the forge over the HTTP API and never pass through git."  # 056b
      root_cause: "The de-branding rewriter is implemented as a git commit-msg hook, so its reach is exactly what git mediates. auto-pr hands --description straight to create_pr with no scrub; forgejo-api.sh and merge-pr have none either. INV-kunot closed the commit-message home of this fact and its statement never named the API home."  # 056b
- op: discuss  # fe5b
  at: '2026-08-26T21:35:22Z'  # fe5b
  by: agent  # fe5b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fe5b
  clock: 2  # fe5b
  nonce: fe5b  # fe5b
  message: "OWNER RULINGS 2026-08-26, recorded before implementation.\n\nPLACEMENT, verbatim: \"the scrub belongs in auto-pr\".\n\nSCOPE, chosen from three options put to the owner: FULL SWEEP, WINDOWED --\nshare the existing rewriter, applied to the first and last N lines rather than\nthe whole body. Rejected: whole-body (maximum coverage, but every false\npositive is a SILENT line deletion, and INV-kunot measured a real one where\n`falcon`, a framework this project ships a catalogue for, mangled a subject and\ndeleted a body line with no marker); and session-identifier-only (zero\nfalse-positive risk but leaves the filed invariant half-satisfied, since prose\nnaming a vendor would still publish).\n\nMATERIAL FINDING THAT SHRINKS THIS ITEM: the window ALREADY EXISTS. The hook\ncarries `body_scan_window=\"${HOOK_BODY_SCAN_WINDOW:-10}\"` (commit-msg:149) and\nimplements exactly the first-N/last-N sweep, with the owner's own INV-kunot\nrationale written out beside it -- vendor self-attribution clusters at the two\nends, the middle of a long body is ordinary technical prose, and a body of\n<= 2*window lines is fully covered so short messages are unaffected. Subject\nand trailers are scanned UNCONDITIONALLY and are not subject to the window.\n\nSO THIS IS EXTRACTION AND WIRING, NOT NEW POLICY. No scrubbing behaviour is\nbeing designed here; the ratified behaviour is being given a second caller.\nThat also sets the acceptance bar: commit-message output must remain\nBYTE-IDENTICAL, and .githooks/test_hooks.sh is the regression proof.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION SHAPE, so the reviewer can check it against the ruling:\n  * Extract the scrub into ONE shared home that both callers source. A second\n    copy is refused on principle -- this project has repeatedly paid for one\n    fact with two homes, and the more destructive consumer holds the weaker\n    rule.\n  * `.githooks/commit-msg` keeps the git-specific parts it alone needs: reading\n    the message file, writing it back, and the DCO check.\n  * `scripts/auto-pr` routes the PR TITLE and DESCRIPTION through the shared\n    scrub before handing them to `create_pr`, on every path that creates a PR\n    (do_pr and flush_queue), not just the first one found.\n\nCARRIED HAZARDS, from the hook's own comments -- an extraction that breaks any\nof these is wrong even if tests pass:\n  * `nocasematch` is LOAD-BEARING and is set ~100 lines before its use; it\n    makes `case` match case-insensitively, which is what lets both\n    `Co-authored-by` and `Co-Authored-By` hit the git-semantic arm.\n  * The key-branded test is written `if [[ ... ]]; then ...; fi` and NOT\n    `[[ ... ]] && key_branded=1`, because the && form returns 1 on a clean key\n    and would become an `exit 1` under `set -e` if that block ever ends a\n    function. Moving this code into a function is EXACTLY the move that arms\n    that landmine.\n  * git-semantic trailer keys (Signed-off-by, Co-authored-by, Co-committed-by)\n    are never renamed, because interpret-trailers and DCO validation key off\n    the exact token.\n\nNOT RULED, and not decided unilaterally: whether the already-published bodies\non #548, #552, #553 and #556 should be edited. That is a forge API write and\nneeds its own authorisation."  # fe5b
- op: discuss  # 8c86
  at: '2026-08-26T21:46:52Z'  # 8c86
  by: agent  # 8c86
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8c86
  clock: 3  # 8c86
  nonce: 8c86  # 8c86
  message: "IMPLEMENTED AND GREEN, NOT PUBLISHED. Branch\njgstern-agent/fix/kuzug-scrub-pr-bodies @ local commit only; no push, no PR,\nbecause scripts/auto-pr and .githooks/** are governance and the #553 approval\ndoes not carry.\n\nWHAT LANDED ON THE BRANCH\n  * .githooks/lib/debrand-message -- the scrub, as a stdin->stdout filter.\n    Kept a STANDALONE SCRIPT, not a sourced function: the code is ~250 lines of\n    top-level bash and one block is written `if [[ ... ]]; then ...; fi`\n    precisely because the && form returns 1 on a clean key, which becomes an\n    `exit 1` under set -e the moment that block ends a function. Wrapping it is\n    the move that arms that landmine.\n  * .githooks/commit-msg -- thinned to the genuinely git-specific parts: the\n    message-file argument, writing back, the DCO gate.\n  * scripts/auto-pr -- _autopr_debrand routes TITLE/DESC (do_pr) and\n    pr_title/pr_desc (flush_queue) through the shared filter. BOTH paths: a fix\n    applied only to do_pr would leave the offline/vPR route publishing\n    unscrubbed, which is this same defect one level down.\n  * Both callers FAIL CLOSED on a missing filter. Publishing is irreversible in\n    the way that matters, so an absent scrub is an error, never a skip.\n\nEVIDENCE\n  * .githooks/test_hooks.sh 42 passed / 0 failed, unchanged from baseline --\n    the proof that extraction moved no ratified behaviour.\n  * tests/test_autopr_debrand.py, 12 tests: filter behaviour, the wiring on\n    both paths, fail-closed, a NEGATIVE CONTROL that clean text is untouched,\n    and two pins that auto-pr carries no SECOND COPY of the scrub.\n  * Affected suite 1625 passed / 0 failed.\n\nLATENT BUG FOUND BY ADDING THE SECOND CALLER, fixed in the same commit. The\ntrailer scan reached line 1, and the trailer regex matches every\nconventional-commit subject, so a ONE-LINE input was classified as BOTH subject\nand trailer and emitted TWICE. Inert for commit messages -- the DCO gate\nguarantees a Signed-off-by line, so there is always a blank for the scan to\nstop at -- but a PR title is one line and hit it every time, injecting a\nnewline that CORRUPTED THE vPR QUEUE JSON (two pre-existing tests failed). The\nscan now stops at line 2: git itself never treats the subject as a trailer.\nNOTE: without the second caller this stays latent and harmless, so if this\nchange is rejected the bug is not urgent -- but it is real and it is in the\nshipped hook.\n\nTHE COST, MEASURED, AND THEN DEMONSTRATED ON THIS WORK ITSELF. A body hit\nDELETES THE WHOLE LINE with no marker. On a 34-line PR body the session URL was\ncaught AND a legitimate line naming a supported web framework was deleted with\nit. The window spares the middle, but a PR body's last lines are its FOOTER --\n\"not in scope\", closing caveats, the session URL -- which is exactly where both\nthe thing-to-scrub and ordinary prose live.\n\nThen the mechanism proved it unprompted: the first draft of this branch's\nCOMMIT MESSAGE named that framework literally while explaining the risk, and\nthe hook deleted that line on commit, leaving a severed sentence -- \"the\nsession URL was caught AND a / middle, but\" -- with nothing marking the\ndeletion. Caught by diffing the intended message against the committed one, not\nby any error. The message was rephrased so it survives its own filter.\n\nOPEN, FOR THE OWNER, both flagged before implementation and still unanswered:\n  1. Whether PR bodies should MARK a replacement in place instead of silently\n     deleting the line. Nothing is lost, the brand still does not publish, and\n     commit-message behaviour is untouched. This is new policy, so it is not\n     being decided here.\n  2. Whether the already-published bodies on #548, #552, #553 and #556 should\n     be edited. That is a forge API write and needs its own authorisation."  # 8c86
